.SH NAME
messq - a lightweight, single-binary queue daemon


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
messq is a lightweight, single-binary message queue for Linux.

.PP
The same binary runs the daemon (serve) and drives it as a client;
every command answers to the same flags, environment variables,
output modes and exit-code contract, so scripts written against one
command keep working against all of them.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for messq

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq version
  messq serve --data-dir /var/lib/messq
  messq verify --deep --data-dir /var/lib/messq
.EE


